      "content": "Proponents argue that vouchers increase competition among schools and give parents of struggling children the freedom to choose better education, which they claim leads to higher student achievement. Opponents counter that the system diverts vital public funds from underfunded public schools, may favor wealthy families who can best navigate the process, and ultimately undermines the collective benefit of a unified public school system. The core disagreement often centers on whether investment in individual choice or fair public support is the more effective way to improve overall educational outcomes.",
